// RS canvas textures.
//
// EMPTY ON PURPOSE. Everything that used to be declared here -- one
// weapon-card canvas, nine in-world panel faces, and one shared drop
// beam -- belonged to the card and billboard system, which is gone.
// Verified before removal: not one of the eleven names was referenced
// anywhere outside this file.
//
// ONE FINDING WORTH KEEPING, because it cost a day to establish and
// would cost another to re-establish. A canvas texture applied to an
// actor via picnum + RF_FLATSPRITE RENDERS NOTHING. Confirmed in the
// running game 2026-08-08 by spawning two identical actors in the same
// tic at the same spot, one on a canvas texture and one on the wall
// texture BROWN1: the wall texture drew, the canvas did not, with a
// valid picnum, alpha 1, bInvisible false, and the correct scaled size
// all printed at spawn.
//
// So if in-world drawable surfaces are ever wanted again, canvases on
// flat sprites are not the route -- that path was never visible, and
// nothing built on it ever worked.
// =====================================================================
